      "grade_ms": 359,
      "final_response": "Tests pass. The bug was an off-by-one check: `l.tokens \u003c= 1` blocked the last available token. The fix is `l.tokens \u003c= 0`, which only denies when there are no tokens remaining. With `burst=3`, all 3 tokens are now consumed, and the 4th call is correctly denied.\n\nFinal `limiter.go`:\n\n```go\npackage rate\n\ntype Limiter struct {\n\ttokens int\n\tburst  int\n}\n\nfunc NewLimiter(burst int) *Limiter {\n\treturn \u0026Limiter{burst: burst, tokens: burst}\n}\n\nfunc (l *Limiter) Allow() bool {\n\tif l.tokens \u003c= 0 {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tl.tokens--\n\treturn true\n}\n```",
